IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-72, TARGETED: the Annual Leave Law, 5711-1951 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two citations in section 27 of the Law (items I1 and I2) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the Law applies, an employee or an employer. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an ordinance as the pages identify it, a reference to a provision of an ordinance, a pointer in the citing words, a citation, a repealing instruction, the places a footnote names, and the page facts of the Interpretation Law. No reference is stated here; they are in an72-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every citation is recorded with two limbs:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument.
-- LATIN LETTERS. The Hebrew of every number and quoted word is on an `ext:` line (read from the deposited page image of an official instrument) or a `src:` line (the deposited excerpt of the consolidation), and the modules type it in Latin letters (tools/translit.py checks the Latin against the Hebrew, line by line):
--   "and-" is the prefix vav with maqaf; a letter alef, bet, gimel or dalet alone in brackets is (a), (b), (c) or (d).
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the instruments'. The English title of each ordinance is a working translation; the identity of an ordinance is a constructor, never the spelling of its title (the 1951 page and the 1965 page spell one title differently).
-- NotChecked is a value, not an absence: it marks a provision the citing words name and this row did not read.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `An ordinance as the pages identify it` IS ONE OF
    `Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)`
    `Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Trial on Indictment)`
    `Labour Department Ordinance, 1943`
    `Factories Ordinance, 1946`

DECLARE `A status in the instruments read` IS ONE OF
    `Repealed by an instrument deposited here`
    `Printed on a page deposited here`
    NotChecked

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page images`
    `official page images, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `official page image of the words as enacted, and the table of instruments touching the Law (NOTES.md section 7; none of them deposited)`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

DECLARE `How a pointer names the Ordinance` IS ONE OF
    `by its title`
    `as the same Ordinance as the pointer before it`

-- A provision of an ordinance as a pair: a section, and a subsection or NOTHING for the whole section.
DECLARE `A provision reference` HAS
    `the ordinance` IS A `An ordinance as the pages identify it`
    `its section` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection, or NOTHING for the whole section` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- One pointer in the citing words: the words that name sections, the ordinance they name and how, and the provisions they name.
DECLARE `A pointer` HAS
    `the words that name the sections, in Latin letters` IS A STRING
    `the ordinance the pointer names` IS A `An ordinance as the pages identify it`
    `the pointer names the Ordinance` IS A `How a pointer names the Ordinance`
    `the provisions the pointer names` IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`

DECLARE `A citation` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the pointers` IS A LIST OF `A pointer`
    `an instruction in the table of instruments touching the Law names section 27` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A repealing instruction` HAS
    `the instrument that repeals` IS A STRING
    `the place of the instruction` IS A STRING
    `the words that name the repealed sections, item by item, in Latin letters` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the provisions it repeals` IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`
    `the issue date its footer prints` IS A DATE
    `the commencement its pages print` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `A footnote naming a place in the Laws of Palestine` HAS
    `the volume of the Laws of Palestine` IS A NUMBER
    `the chapter of the Laws of Palestine` IS A NUMBER
    `the page of the Laws of Palestine` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `A footnote naming a Gazette supplement` HAS
    `the Gazette number` IS A NUMBER
    `the supplement number` IS A NUMBER
    `the page of the Gazette supplement` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `A printed section of the Interpretation Law` HAS
    `the section printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the issue of Sefer HaChukim` IS A NUMBER
    `the printed page of the section` IS A NUMBER
    `the issue date the footer of the section prints` IS A DATE

DECLARE `A later instrument that touches the Interpretation Law` HAS
    `the later issue of Sefer HaChukim` IS A NUMBER
    `the later issue date` IS A DATE
    `the sections of the Interpretation Law it names` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- ===== THE QUESTIONS. Each takes a value from an72-cross-references.l4. =====

-- A repealed subsection reaches a cited subsection when the repealed one is NOTHING (the whole section is repealed) or the two are the same subsection. The two sides are typed as (section, subsection or NOTHING) pairs and compared on the section, never by string equality of "10" and "10 (1)".
GIVEN rs IS A MAYBE STRING
      ps IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the repealed subsection reaches the cited subsection` MEANS (rs EQUALS NOTHING) OR (rs EQUALS ps)

GIVEN r IS A `A provision reference`
      p IS A `A provision reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` MEANS (r's `the ordinance` EQUALS p's `the ordinance`) AND (r's `its section` EQUALS p's `its section`) AND (`the repealed subsection reaches the cited subsection` (r's `its subsection, or NOTHING for the whole section`) (p's `its subsection, or NOTHING for the whole section`))

GIVEN a IS A `A provision reference`
      b IS A `A provision reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two references are to the same provision` MEANS (a's `the ordinance` EQUALS b's `the ordinance`) AND (a's `its section` EQUALS b's `its section`) AND (a's `its subsection, or NOTHING for the whole section` EQUALS b's `its subsection, or NOTHING for the whole section`)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision reference`
      rs IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some repealed provision in the list reaches the cited provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` r p) OR (`some repealed provision in the list reaches the cited provision` p rest)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision reference`
      instructions IS A LIST OF `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER instructions
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN i FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (`some repealed provision in the list reaches the cited provision` p (i's `the provisions it repeals`)) OR (`some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` p rest)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision reference`
      printed IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cited provision is among the printed provisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER printed
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN q FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (`the two references are to the same provision` q p) OR (`the cited provision is among the printed provisions` p rest)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A pointer`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision reference`
`the provisions the pointers name` MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN q FOLLOWED BY rest THEN append (q's `the provisions the pointer names`) (`the provisions the pointers name` rest)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision reference`
`the provisions the citing words name` MEANS `the provisions the pointers name` (c's `the pointers`)

GIVEN cited IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`
      instructions IS A LIST OF `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision reference`
`the listed provisions that a listed instruction repeals` MEANS
    CONSIDER cited
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` p instructions
        THEN p FOLLOWED BY (`the listed provisions that a listed instruction repeals` rest instructions)
        ELSE `the listed provisions that a listed instruction repeals` rest instructions

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
      instructions IS A LIST OF `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision reference`
`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` MEANS `the listed provisions that a listed instruction repeals` (`the provisions the citing words name` c) instructions

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
      instructions IS A LIST OF `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no provision the citing words name is repealed by a listed instruction` MEANS null (`the provisions the citing words name that a listed instruction repeals` c instructions)

GIVEN ps IS A LIST OF `A provision reference`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the section numbers of the listed provisions` MEANS
    CONSIDER ps
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (p's `its section`) FOLLOWED BY (`the section numbers of the listed provisions` rest)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision reference`
      instructions IS A LIST OF `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A `A status in the instruments read`
`the status of the cited provision` MEANS
    IF `some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` p instructions
    THEN `Repealed by an instrument deposited here`
    ELSE NotChecked

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS (c's `limb (a) holds`) AND (c's `limb (b) holds`)

GIVEN a IS A `A footnote naming a place in the Laws of Palestine`
      b IS A `A footnote naming a place in the Laws of Palestine`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two footnotes name the same place` MEANS (a's `the volume of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS b's `the volume of the Laws of Palestine`) AND (a's `the chapter of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS b's `the chapter of the Laws of Palestine`) AND (a's `the page of the Laws of Palestine` EQUALS b's `the page of the Laws of Palestine`)

GIVEN a IS A `A footnote naming a Gazette supplement`
      b IS A `A footnote naming a Gazette supplement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two footnotes name the same Gazette issue and supplement` MEANS (a's `the Gazette number` EQUALS b's `the Gazette number`) AND (a's `the supplement number` EQUALS b's `the supplement number`)

GIVEN l IS A `A later instrument that touches the Interpretation Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the later instrument names section 25` MEANS elem 25 (l's `the sections of the Interpretation Law it names`)

-- The day a repeal took effect is not given by the pages this row reads (the date a footer prints is the date of the issue), so the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN i IS A `A repealing instruction`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the repeal took effect` MEANS NOTHING
